ice:{name:'Ice crater',x:-20,z:12,gain:{air:20},text:'Drive the rover to a crater with frozen water. Splitting water makes oxygen, so this gives the crew 20 air. Scientists really have found buried ice on Mars.',found:'Water ice! The crew split some into oxygen: +20 air.'},
lava:{name:'Lava tube',x:19,z:-16,gain:{rad:20},text:'Drive the rover to a cave left by old lava. Rock overhead blocks the Sun’s rays, so scientists think such caves could shelter people. The crew rests there and gains 20 Safety.',found:'A natural cave! Rock overhead blocks radiation: +20 Safety.'},
probe:{name:'Old lander',x:24,z:12,gain:{rp:3},text:'Drive the rover to a lander that arrived many years ago. Its instruments kept a weather log. Reading it gives 3 research points. Engineers study old hardware to learn how machines last on Mars.',found:'The old lander still had its weather log: +3 research points.'},
canyon:{name:'Canyon rim',x:4,z:-24,gain:{rp:2},exposed:true,text:'Drive the rover to the edge of a canyon where rock layers are stacked like pages in a book. Each layer is a different time in Mars history: +2 research points. It is open ground, so the trip costs extra Safety when the Sun is active.',found:'Layer upon layer of rock: a timeline of Mars. +2 research points.'},
